    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s lineup for June 23, 2026, is headlined by **Bryson Stott**, who leads the squad with a 68.78 daily efficiency score. Despite the suboptimal #8 spot in the order, **Bryson Stott** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost against Zack Littell and a favorable platoon matchup. **Cal Raleigh** remains a top-tier play at 68.07, capitalizing on the combination of a high-value #2 slot and wind conditions out at the stadium. We are also projecting significant upside from **Luis Arraez**, **Matt Chapman**, and **Jung Hoo Lee**, all of whom are facing Aaron Civale; their scores are bolstered by a high SP skill factor and, in the cases of **Luis Arraez** and **Jung Hoo Lee**, a meaningful boost from wind conditions. **Daulton Varsho** continues to be a core asset, anchored by a strong 65.84 score driven by a favorable park and solid dynamic platoon metrics.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was leaving **Geraldo Perdomo** on the pine. With a score of 55.34, he was the primary candidate to displace **Jeremiah Jackson** (56.58). While **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits from an assumed #2 order placement, the optimization engine favored the higher raw efficiency of **Jeremiah Jackson**, despite the latter\u2019s lower slot in the order, because of the matchup against Ryan Johnson. Managers should keep a close eye on the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all players today; if the actual batting orders deviate from our projections, particularly for the middle-infield cohort like **Tyler Freeman**, efficiency scores will need immediate re-evaluation. While **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains sidelined, we are closely monitoring the bottom of the order for any signs of defensive substitutions that could threaten the viability of the lower-scoring plays like **Jeremiah Jackson** and **Masyn Winn**.",
